{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The fire-offerings of YHWH</b> — these are the consecrated portions of the Sanctuary. <b>His inheritance</b> — these are the consecrated portions of the borderlands: priestly gifts and tithes. But an absolute inheritance he shall not have among his brothers. And in the Sifrei they expounded: <b>'and he shall have no inheritance'</b> — this is the inheritance of the remainder. <b>'among his brothers'</b> — this is the inheritance of the seven. And I do not know what this means.\n\nNow it appears to me that the land of Canaan from across the Jordan onward is called the land of the five nations, while that of Sihon and Og is two nations — the Amorite and the Canaanite — and the 'inheritance of the remainder' serves to include the Kenite and the Kenizzite and the Kadmonite.\n\nFurther, I found in the words of Rabbi Kalonymus: thus we read in the Sifrei (Shofetim 164): <b>'and he shall have no inheritance'</b> — these are the inheritance of the five. <b>'among his brothers'</b> — these are the inheritance of the seven. The inheritance of five tribes and the inheritance of seven tribes. And since Moses and Joshua apportioned inheritance to only five tribes — for Moses gave inheritance to Reuben and Gad and half the tribe of Manasseh, and Joshua gave inheritance to Judah and Ephraim and half the tribe of Manasseh — while the other seven took their portions by themselves after the death of Joshua, therefore he mentioned five separately and seven separately.\n\nAll this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 18:1). And I have already explained the main principle in the pericope of <i>Qadesh Li</i> (Exodus 13:5): that the inheritance of the five nations mentioned in the verse 'When YHWH brings you to the land of the Canaanite and the Hittite and the Amorite and the Hivite and the Jebusite, which He swore to your fathers to give you, a land flowing with milk and honey' — these are the essential inheritance of Israel, whose land was flowing with milk and honey. But the two remaining ones, namely the Perizzite and the Girgashite — their land is not flowing with milk and honey and is not obligated in first fruits. Therefore Scripture states regarding the Levites that they shall not take a portion with Israel in the essence of their inheritance, in the good land which is the inheritance of the five, nor in the inheritance of the seven, which are the two remaining ones, even though their land is not good and is not so esteemed in the eyes of Israel. And this matter is clear from the proofs that I have written there."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "Ramban first offers his own guess at the meaning of 'inheritance of the remainder' and 'inheritance of the seven,' then cites a variant reading from the Sifrei via Rabbi Kalonymus, and notes that all the preceding explanation follows Rashi's interpretation. The paragraph beginning 'And I have already explained' transitions to his own fuller discussion previously given in his commentary on Exodus 13:5."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:51:33.901734092Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}